<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tamesna</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tamesna is the historical name of the Atlantic coastal plain of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> between the Bou Regreg river at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sale">Salé</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rabat">Rabat</a> and the Oum Er-Rbia river. From the 8th century it was the heartland of the Barghawata, whose state was destroyed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohads</a>. The Almohads and later dynasties resettled it with Arab tribes, and it corresponds largely to the modern Chaouia region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tamesna.jpg" alt="Tamesna" width="320" height="262" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Omar-toons · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Barghouata_Carte.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
